From: tesla-ble-api
Subject: [PATCH] tesla-control: configure BLE credentials in interactive mode

Upstream `tesla-control` only calls configureFlags() when a command argument is
present on the command line. Started with NO command (i.e. the interactive
shell, which this project relies on for a persistent session), the config falls
back to requiring an OAuth token and the session fails at startup with:

    could not load token: ... keyring ...

This patch configures BLE credentials (private key + VIN, no OAuth) explicitly
when the interactive shell is launched with -ble, so the persistent session
works with just the enrolled key and VIN.

Base: teslamotors/vehicle-command @ d6239bf (adjust context if upstream moves).
Apply from the repo root with:  git apply patches/0001-*.patch
            (or)                patch -p1 < patches/0001-*.patch
Then rebuild:  go build -o ~/bin/tesla-control ./cmd/tesla-control
And re-grant:  sudo setcap 'cap_net_admin,cap_net_raw+eip' ~/bin/tesla-control
---
 cmd/tesla-control/main.go | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cmd/tesla-control/main.go b/cmd/tesla-control/main.go
index 046ad6e..f6b763d 100644
--- a/cmd/tesla-control/main.go
+++ b/cmd/tesla-control/main.go
@@ -152,6 +152,12 @@ func main() {
 			writeErr("Missing required flag: %s", err)
 			return
 		}
+	} else if forceBLE {
+		// Interactive shell over BLE: no command arg means configureFlags is
+		// never called, so the config would default to requiring an OAuth
+		// token. Configure BLE credentials explicitly (private key + VIN, no
+		// OAuth) so the persistent interactive session works without a token.
+		config.Flags = cli.FlagBLE | cli.FlagPrivateKey | cli.FlagVIN
 	}

 	if err := config.LoadCredentials(); err != nil {
